        "subject": "History tells grace decisions in its own words; the console names a paid end's message by its outcome",
        "body": "History tells grace decisions in its own words; the console names a paid end's message by its outcome\n\n- The subscription history knew neither 0099 event kind: a grace started and a period that ended with none left both\n  read \"Change recorded\", followed by the server's English note, in French and Arabic alike. grace_started and\n  grace_unavailable now have their own words in EN/FR/AR and are told from catalogue sentences with the period end the\n  server recorded (periodEndAfter), in the business's zone and isolated in Arabic, as the trial's events are; an event\n  without a period end says so without a date. The server's note is no longer shown for them.\n- The console's message log and a business's messages named both paid-end messages \"paid period ended\". With the\n  row's variant they now say \"paid period ended — grace started\" or \"— no grace left\" (EN/FR/AR). The portal's\n  summary is unchanged: its status panel already states the grace outcome.\n\nFound on the real-API screenshots of the rehearsal. Tests: every kind has words in each language (the two added);\ngrace told in French and Arabic with the zone's date and never the server's note; both variant names in the console;\nthe source rule extended to the grace kinds. Gates: typecheck; Vitest 33 files, 534/534; the three production builds\nrefused without their inputs; full, public and portal previews with 0 broken links and the bundle audits passing;\nPlaywright full 138/138, public 148/148, portal 34/34.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PLhoUhSVGTwofTQRXsJNof\n",
